---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ProjectInvitation from '../components/ProjectInvitation.astro';
import { getPublishedPieces } from '../lib/lab';
import Byline from '../components/Byline.astro';
import PublicationDate from '../components/PublicationDate.astro';
import { hadiProfile } from '../lib/people';
import '../styles/visitor.css';
const pieces = await getPublishedPieces();
---
<SiteLayout title="About Fidret | Purpose, people and work" description="Fidret is an emerging engineering company developing its first practice in Physical AI. Meet Hadi Abou Daya and explore the work behind Trust earned." canonical="https://fidret.com/project/">
  <main tabindex="-1" id="main">
    <header class="visitor-hero shell">
      <h1>About Fidret</h1>
      <p class="visitor-lead">An emerging engineering company, built around useful work and the judgment behind it.</p>
      <p>We build software experiments and explore system designs. Our aim is to earn trust through what people experience when working with us: clear thinking, honest commitments and work they can use.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="about-person inverse"><div class="visitor-split shell">
      <h2>Hadi Abou Daya</h2>
      <div><p>{hadiProfile.role}. {hadiProfile.background}</p><p>Hadi is building Fidret and authors its published Lab work on Physical AI, agent workflows and AI-assisted software delivery. His professional background is distinct from Fidret’s own projects and explorations.</p><div class="visitor-actions"><a class="text-link" href="/people/hadi/">Hadi’s work and role</a><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">Talk about an idea</a></div></div>
    </div></section>
    <section class="visitor-split shell">
      <h2>Starting with Physical AI.</h2>
      <div><p>How can a system use information from the world around it to help people make decisions or operate equipment? What should it do when that information is old, incomplete or conflicting?</p><p>Those questions guide our first practice. Related work on agents and software explores how to check results, set clear permissions and recover when something goes wrong.</p><a class="text-link" href="/work/">Explore the questions and what we made</a></div>
    </section>
    <section class="visitor-split shell">
      <h2>Trust earned.</h2>
      <div><p>That is Fidret’s chosen meaning. The name is inspired by the Latin <i lang="la">fīdere</i>, to trust or rely upon.</p><p>For us, it means understanding a situation before choosing a technology, making commitments clear and showing what a result does and does not establish. Sometimes good judgment means changing direction or stopping.</p><a class="text-link" href="/charter/">Read the company charter</a></div>
    </section>
    <section class="visitor-split shell">
      <h2>Work someone else can understand and continue.</h2>
      <div><p>We keep decisions, responsibilities and checks alongside the implementation, so another person can understand how it works and what still needs attention.</p><p>AI agents can assist. Named people remain responsible for the work and its consequences.</p><a class="text-link" href="/approach/">Our working approach</a></div>
    </section>
    {pieces.length > 0 && <section class="about-publications shell" aria-labelledby="publications-title"><div class="visitor-section-heading"><h2 id="publications-title">From the Lab</h2><p>Each published piece names its actual contributors.</p></div><div class="about-publication-list">{pieces.map(piece=><article><h3><a href={`/lab/${piece.data.slug}/`}>{piece.data.title}</a></h3><p>{piece.data.summary}</p><p class="work-kind"><PublicationDate value={piece.data.published}/> · By <Byline authors={piece.data.authors}/></p></article>)}</div></section>}
    <ProjectInvitation />
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
